00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:08.050
this is a very common workflow.

00:04:08.050 --> 00:04:11.220
The sales associate needs
to have the same pitch

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:15.155
deck that they tweak slightly
for various customers.

00:04:15.155 --> 00:04:19.750
This customization's not fast,
and often prone to human error.

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:22.060
You make a copy of
the template, change

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:25.870
the name of the customer,
the corresponding data,

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:29.592
and then you do that one slide
deck at a time, over and over

00:04:29.592 --> 00:04:31.060
again.

00:04:31.060 --> 00:04:35.220
Google Slides has an API to
help streamline and error-proof

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:35.800
this process.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:43.140
