REST API and Apps Script API

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:45.440
to give users
programmatic access

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:49.070
to create and update
presentations in Slides

00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:51.340
from any data source.

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:54.880
Your team can build
ready-to-go presentations

00:04:54.880 --> 00:04:58.930
to turn business data
into presentations,

00:04:58.930 --> 00:05:03.240
and streamline the
slide-creation process.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:07.160
With these APIs, you can use
your internal tools, templates,

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:09.630
and your customer data
to fill in placeholders

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:13.220
across various
versions of the pitch

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:15.037
decks you need with
just one click.

00:05:18.693 --> 00:05:21.111
While templates give you a
head start with formatting

00:05:21.111 --> 00:05:24.120
and layout, what about
getting a head start

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:26.970
on the content in
your presentation?

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:30.392
To help ensure you always have
the most up-to-date content,

00:05:30.392 --> 00:05:34.360
we built a feature
called linked slides.

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:36.240
We've built this
feature because we

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:40.140
know convincing and
powerful presentations often

00:05:40.140 --> 00:05:43.440
have data and slides
from other sources.

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:47.084
And we have feedback that this
is a common workflow for many

00:05:47.084 --> 00:05:49.300
of you.

00:05:49.300 --> 00:05:51.025
You have a few
slides from old decks

00:05:51.025 --> 00:05:53.790
that you want to reuse
in a new presentation,

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:55.680
over and over again.

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:59.250
But repeatedly copying
slides from one presentation

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:02.430
to another as they get
updated is a major time sink,

00:06:02.430 --> 00:06:06.810
and can be easy to miss
subtle, but important, changes.

00:06:06.810 --> 00:06:10.110
Now, with linked
slides, you can link

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:13.290
and sync slides from
multiple presentations.

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:15.000
You know they need
updated because

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:18.510
in the right-hand corner,
you'll see an update button.

00:06:18.510 --> 00:06:21.703
This way, you can maintain
a single source of truth,

00:06:21.703 --> 00:06:24.770
and update content
in new presentations

00:06:24.770 --> 00:06:27.060
to match your source
of truth with just

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:29.180
the click of a button.

00:06:29.180 --> 00:06:31.730
This can be great for
important presentations

00:06:31.730 --> 00:06:33.440
like quarterly business reviews.

00:06:36.840 --> 00:06:40.260
We also expanded the same
linking functionality

00:06:40.260 --> 00:06:43.110
to content within slides.

00:06:43.110 --> 00:06:46.560
We know that a lot of
business data lives in Sheets.

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:49.740
So we expanded this
linking functionality such

00:06:49.740 --> 00:06:53.550
that you can also link tables
and charts that you copy over

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:55.230
from Sheets files.

00:06:55.230 --> 00:06:56.970
When the table in
Sheets is updated,

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:59.810
or the corresponding
chart is updated,

00:06:59.810 --> 00:07:01.760
you'll see that
same update button

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:04.980
in the right-hand corner
of the table or chart,

00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:07.062
telling you that
there is new data

00:07:07.062 --> 00:07:08.998
to pull into your presentation.

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:17.980
If the original chart or table
changes without being linked,

00:07:17.980 --> 00:07:20.795
it can be tedious and
time-consuming to replace it

00:07:20.795 --> 00:07:22.939
in each and every file.

00:07:22.939 --> 00:07:24.480
This feature saves
you valuable time,

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:27.800
and we make it possible to
update your chart with just

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:30.480
a single click, without
the need to ever leave

00:07:30.480 --> 00:07:33.120
the context of your
document or presentation.

00:07:36.396 --> 00:07:37.770
Now that you have
a good starting

00:07:37.770 --> 00:07:41.670
point with a consistent
format and slides,

00:07:41.670 --> 00:07:45.210
charts and tables linked
from your previous work,

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:48.030
you're ready to bring in your
teammates to get their insights

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:49.830
and feedback.

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:52.649
Let's see how Google Slides
can help you collaborate.

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:59.000
Google Slides keeps all of
its content in the cloud.

00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:02.450
This means that there is no
need to create multiple versions

00:08:02.450 --> 00:08:07.270
of decks, emailed back and
forth between teammates with

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:14.010
confusing version names
like v1, v1.2, v2, v2 final.

00:08:14.010 --> 00:08:15.230
We've all seen these.

00:08:15.230 --> 00:08:19.590
And it can be confusing to
know who updated what and when.

00:08:19.590 --> 00:08:21.643
Syncing the content
from multiple people

00:08:21.643 --> 00:08:25.708
in multiple versions of
files can be a job in itself.

00:08:25.708 --> 00:08:28.300
With Google Slides,
the whole team

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:32.990
works from the same file
with realtime collaboration.

00:08:32.990 --> 00:08:35.720
What you see on screen
is how collaboration

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:37.909
works in Google Slides.

00:08:37.909 --> 00:08:41.870
Multiple people are making
changes in real time.

00:08:41.870 --> 00:08:44.730
And even if they're working
in different time zones,

00:08:44.730 --> 00:08:47.068
in different parts
of the word, you

00:08:47.068 --> 00:08:49.700
don't have to deal
with version roulette,

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:52.141
because everyone's
working on the same file.

00:08:56.290 --> 00:08:59.040
But collaboration in Slides
is more than just content

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:00.500
on a presentation.

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:03.120
Comments in Slides also
allow your team members

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:07.900
to leave suggestions or
notes on what to edit or add.

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:10.830
You can also assign an
action item to someone

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:12.900
by mentioning their
name in a comment

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:16.270
and checking the
Action Item box.

00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:18.460
The assignee will get an email.

00:09:18.460 --> 00:09:20.680
And the next time
they enter the file,

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:23.340
they'll see the action
items clearly highlighted

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:26.840
with a blue bar.

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:32.870
This allows for clear task
delegation and faster teamwork.

00:09:32.870 --> 00:09:34.800
That's because all
of the collaborators

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:37.400
know who needs to
contribute and where

00:09:37.400 --> 00:09:39.052
their contributions are needed.

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:46.510
We also know that teams are
often working on the go,

00:09:46.510 --> 00:09:49.720
while commuting to the
office or on business trips.

00:09:49.720 --> 00:09:52.240
To help accommodate
this, we continually

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:54.520
invest in our
mobile apps to make

00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:59.089
sure you have access to all the
functionality you need wherever

00:09:59.089 --> 00:10:00.540
you are.

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:04.000
Our apps are available
on both iOS and Android.

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:06.980
And the same realtime
collaboration features,

00:10:06.980 --> 00:10:10.740
along with all the formatting
and content creation tools

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:14.530
you could need to create
a quick presentation,

00:10:14.530 --> 00:10:17.940
make a minor edit, or
respond to a comment.

00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:21.160
Our mobile apps also have some
unique functionality that's

00:10:21.160 --> 00:10:24.130
optimized for being on-the-go.

00:10:24.130 --> 00:10:27.026
You can sync presentations so
they're available on the app

00:10:27.026 --> 00:10:30.606
while offline, and use
the mobile app Present

00:10:30.606 --> 00:10:33.340
mode to turn your phone
into a presentation remote.

00:10:39.450 --> 00:10:42.150
Apart from
collaborators, we know

00:10:42.150 --> 00:10:46.438
that stakeholders and approvers
are often part of the process

00:10:46.438 --> 00:10:48.246
to create a presentation.

00:10:48.246 --> 00:10:51.436
You often need to get
your presentation approved

00:10:51.436 --> 00:10:56.368
by stakeholders in various
functions like legal and PR.

00:10:56.368 --> 00:10:59.640
The combination of Google
Slides and Google Drive

00:10:59.640 --> 00:11:01.520
can help with this.

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:03.680
Without G Suite,
you would probably

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:06.410
download the slide
shows as PDFs,

00:11:06.410 --> 00:11:10.360
then use project-tracking tools
to collect formal approvals

00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:11.600
and sign-offs.

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:15.340
While that would technically
work, if any of the approvers

00:11:15.340 --> 00:11:17.800
asked for a change
in the presentation,

00:11:17.800 --> 00:11:21.730
you would need to produce new
copies of the files or PDFs

00:11:21.730 --> 00:11:24.340
and re-send them for approvals.

00:11:24.340 --> 00:11:28.840
As I said earlier, version
roulette isn't fun for anyone.

00:11:28.840 --> 00:11:31.360
With G Suite, this
approval workflow

00:11:31.360 --> 00:11:33.880
is a whole lot more streamlined.

00:11:33.880 --> 00:11:36.940
We recently announced
Drive's upcoming

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:40.480
document-centric
workflows feature,

00:11:40.480 --> 00:11:43.420
which will allow users
to get formal approvals

00:11:43.420 --> 00:11:45.590
on their files.

00:11:45.590 --> 00:11:48.890
With this feature, you can
submit slide decks for approval

00:11:48.890 --> 00:11:51.170
from specific coworkers.

00:11:51.170 --> 00:11:54.950
Upon doing so, the file
gets locked, and shared,

00:11:54.950 --> 00:11:57.400
and sent to the approvers.

00:11:57.400 --> 00:12:00.780
After the file's
approved, it stays locked.

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:02.925
If someone looks at the
file after it's approved,

00:12:02.925 --> 00:12:05.700
they'll be able to tell
clearly it has been approved,

00:12:05.700 --> 00:12:08.260
and that's the final version.

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:11.240
This lightweight workflow
tool can powerfully

00:12:11.240 --> 00:12:13.880
streamline company
processes and will soon

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:16.382
be available in an
early adopter's program.

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:25.680
Along the same lines, when
you have many stakeholders

00:12:25.680 --> 00:12:28.260
and collaborators, it can
be really helpful to track

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:30.550
their progress.

00:12:30.550 --> 00:12:33.700
With other, legacy
presentation tools,

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:37.330
after you send your presentation
to a teammate, you have no idea

00:12:37.330 --> 00:12:40.090
if or when they looked at it.

00:12:40.090 --> 00:12:43.630
It can be hard to understand
who has seen what,

00:12:43.630 --> 00:12:46.390
and this can slow down teamwork.

00:12:46.390 --> 00:12:48.734
Google Slides now
offers the ability

00:12:48.734 --> 00:12:51.450
to view collaborator activity.

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:53.400
The Activity
dashboard allows you

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:56.620
to see which collaborators
viewed your slide deck

00:12:56.620 --> 00:12:59.730
and when, giving you the
power to track progress

00:12:59.730 --> 00:13:02.520
on the project with
many moving parts.

00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:04.850
You can find the Activity
Dashboard in the Tools

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:07.320
drop-down in the main menu.

00:13:07.320 --> 00:13:09.330
With this tool,
you can understand

00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:12.770
which of your teammates have
seen your latest revision,

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:14.900
and who needs to be pinged
to stay in the loop.

00:13:21.300 --> 00:13:25.510
Once the core parts of your
presentation, like the message,

00:13:25.510 --> 00:13:29.560
data, visuals are all ready,
you start worrying about

00:13:29.560 --> 00:13:31.630
the fine-grained details--

00:13:31.630 --> 00:13:33.490
the polish that makes
your presentation

00:13:33.490 --> 00:13:39.710
feel professional and tells the
story best for your audience.

00:13:39.710 --> 00:13:43.670
Google Slides has some great
tools to help with this.

00:13:43.670 --> 00:13:45.946
As you and your
collaborators add content,

00:13:45.946 --> 00:13:48.320
you will likely
need to rearrange

00:13:48.320 --> 00:13:50.660
the layout of your slides.

00:13:50.660 --> 00:13:52.910
With the power of
machine intelligence,

00:13:52.910 --> 00:13:55.880
we built the Explore
feature in Slides,

00:13:55.880 --> 00:13:58.850
so you can just drop your
content on the slide,

00:13:58.850 --> 00:14:00.710
and with a couple
of clicks, you'll

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:02.690
have slides that
look so good, people

00:14:02.690 --> 00:14:07.260
will think you hired a
design agency for them.

00:14:07.260 --> 00:14:09.260
We match slide
themes and layouts

00:14:09.260 --> 00:14:11.012
to best fit your content.

00:14:11.012 --> 00:14:16.820
There's no cropping, resizing,
or reformatting required.

00:14:16.820 --> 00:14:18.630
This Explore tool
is so compelling

00:14:18.630 --> 00:14:21.673
because it really does
save time by taking away

00:14:21.673 --> 00:14:23.525
mundane formatting tasks.

00:14:26.310 --> 00:14:29.880
We've seen that people who use
Explore to select their layouts

00:14:29.880 --> 00:14:32.280
save over 60% of
the time that they

00:14:32.280 --> 00:14:34.310
would have spent formatting.

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:37.820
So even if design
isn't your expertise,

00:14:37.820 --> 00:14:39.830
rest assured that
Slides can help

00:14:39.830 --> 00:14:45.880
make sure you have a beautiful
presentation to be proud of.

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:48.260
And although Slides
Explore is great,

00:14:48.260 --> 00:14:50.300
it needs you to
supply the content.

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:54.360
And we know that another problem
in creating presentations

00:14:54.360 --> 00:14:56.280
is finding the right
visuals or stock

00:14:56.280 --> 00:15:01.570
photography that help deliver
the message to your audience.

00:15:01.570 --> 00:15:04.960
Luckily, Slides has a
platform to help with that.

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:07.060
In Google Slides,
we have a feature

00:15:07.060 --> 00:15:09.290
called Add-ons that
help you source

00:15:09.290 --> 00:15:13.360
these high-quality visuals
from a variety of sources.

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:15.862
Previously, I spoke about APIs.

00:15:15.862 --> 00:15:17.860
Apps Script is one
of these, and it's

00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:21.160
an open platform that
allows any developer

00:15:21.160 --> 00:15:26.800
to create and publish add-ons
that can be added to Slides.

00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:29.590
As a result, we have
a rich add-on store

00:15:29.590 --> 00:15:33.060
with a variety of functionality.

00:15:33.060 --> 00:15:34.840
In the add-on
store, you can find

00:15:34.840 --> 00:15:39.070
tools that help you build
more powerful presentations.

00:15:39.070 --> 00:15:42.170
These add-ons can enable
you to source beautiful,

00:15:42.170 --> 00:15:46.620
full-bleed pictures, use
advanced formatting tools,

00:15:46.620 --> 00:15:52.035
or include diagrams you created
in programs outside of G Suite.

00:15:52.035 --> 00:15:57.990
For example, you can
search for and add pictures

00:15:57.990 --> 00:16:00.780
from Adobe Stock
right in Slides.

00:16:00.780 --> 00:16:04.530
Or you can use the
Shutterstock add-on,

00:16:04.530 --> 00:16:08.160
adding customized
photos within Slides.

00:16:08.160 --> 00:16:11.940
Teams can benefit from even more
powerful capabilities in Slides

00:16:11.940 --> 00:16:16.338
with additional add-ons
from Balsamiq, Lucidchart,

00:16:16.338 --> 00:16:20.610
Pear Deck, Noun
Project, and Unsplash.

00:16:20.610 --> 00:16:22.720
These tools help
bring your content

00:16:22.720 --> 00:16:26.650
that's external to Slides
directly into your G Suite

00:16:26.650 --> 00:16:27.350
workflows.

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:33.970
Google Slides also has
several native tools

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:38.700
to help with the polish you need
to get your deck just right.

00:16:38.700 --> 00:16:41.100
One of the areas
we've been focusing

00:16:41.100 --> 00:16:43.680
is increased font support.

00:16:43.680 --> 00:16:45.690
We know fonts matter.

00:16:45.690 --> 00:16:47.808
There are some fonts that
are good for documents

00:16:47.808 --> 00:16:49.784
that are read on
a personal screen,

00:16:49.784 --> 00:16:52.350
while others are good
on the big screen.

00:16:52.350 --> 00:16:53.898
And different fonts
can really help

00:16:53.898 --> 00:16:58.280
you to find the tone and
narrative of your presentation.

00:16:58.280 --> 00:17:02.820
Today, in Google Slides, you
can choose from over 800 fonts

00:17:02.820 --> 00:17:05.450
via the More Fonts menu.

00:17:05.450 --> 00:17:08.640
In this menu, you can
preview our diverse catalog

00:17:08.640 --> 00:17:11.720
of fonts, which supports
62 languages, including

00:17:11.720 --> 00:17:16.920
non-latin scripts like
Cyrillic and [INAUDIBLE]..

00:17:16.920 --> 00:17:20.905
Once you find fonts you
like in the More Fonts menu,

00:17:20.905 --> 00:17:23.690
you can add them
to My Fonts List.

00:17:23.690 --> 00:17:25.970
And once they're in
your My Fonts List,

00:17:25.970 --> 00:17:29.168
you have quick access to those
fonts in the Font drop-down.

00:17:33.452 --> 00:17:36.760
Another great native design
tool that Google Slides offers

00:17:36.760 --> 00:17:38.720
is the Slide Master.

00:17:38.720 --> 00:17:40.430
This is an advanced
feature that allows

00:17:40.430 --> 00:17:42.870
you to control all
of the information

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:49.930
about theme, layout, background,
color, fonts, and positioning

00:17:49.930 --> 00:17:52.940
of all the slides in your deck.

00:17:52.940 --> 00:17:55.700
Using the Slide Master
can be an easy way

00:17:55.700 --> 00:17:58.890
to perform bulk updates
in your presentation,

00:17:58.890 --> 00:18:03.710
or to ensure new slides always
have the right starting point.

00:18:03.710 --> 00:18:05.480
By using the Slide
Master, you can

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:08.580
make sure the default
fonts, colors,

00:18:08.580 --> 00:18:10.940
and placeholders on
your layouts are always

00:18:10.940 --> 00:18:13.280
set-up to look
great, helping you

00:18:13.280 --> 00:18:16.990
create professional
presentations quickly.

00:18:16.990 --> 00:18:20.040
It's also great to use the Slide
Master when creating templates

00:18:20.040 --> 00:18:21.697
for your company
that you'll then

00:18:21.697 --> 00:18:24.030
upload to the template gallery
that I mentioned earlier.

00:18:28.680 --> 00:18:30.930
While the Slide Master
is great for making

00:18:30.930 --> 00:18:34.170
wide-reaching changes, we
know that for certain slides,

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:37.480
you care about each
and every pixel.

00:18:37.480 --> 00:18:40.170
Aligning an object or
a text box perfectly

00:18:40.170 --> 00:18:44.960
can be tedious and
difficult. So Google Slides

00:18:44.960 --> 00:18:49.090
offer rulers, as well as static
guides, to help with consistent

00:18:49.090 --> 00:18:52.380
placement and alignment
throughout a presentation.

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:56.070
You can turn on rules and
guides in the View menu.

00:18:56.070 --> 00:19:00.120
Once they're on, you can
right-click to add new guides,

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:04.127
and drag guides to the exact
location you need them to be.

00:19:04.127 --> 00:19:05.960
The guides will show
it to all of the slides

00:19:05.960 --> 00:19:09.980
in the presentation so that
text boxes and other objects

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:12.250
will snap to the location
that you care about,

00:19:12.250 --> 00:19:14.744
and you can ensure that
they're all aligned across all

00:19:14.744 --> 00:19:16.656
of the slides in your deck.

00:19:20.960 --> 00:19:22.650
Now that you and
your collaborators

00:19:22.650 --> 00:19:25.640
have added all of
your content and data,

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:27.830
gotten the approvals
needed, and everything

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:29.320
is polished and
buttoned-up, you're

00:19:29.320 --> 00:19:31.260
ready to present your work.

00:19:34.660 --> 00:19:36.760
Whether you're presenting
from your mobile device

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:41.410
or your laptop, via G Suite
Meet, or on a big screen,

00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:45.460
the Presenter view in Google
Slides gives you as a present

00:19:45.460 --> 00:19:48.220
a special view into
the presentation.

00:19:48.220 --> 00:19:51.550
The Presenter view helps
you be a better presenter

00:19:51.550 --> 00:19:57.070
with features like speaker
notes, quick slide navigation,

00:19:57.070 --> 00:19:59.350
and a laser pointer.

00:19:59.350 --> 00:20:01.930
Speaker notes allow you
to craft your message

00:20:01.930 --> 00:20:03.760
and have access to
all the notes that you

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:06.430
need to give a great
presentation, right

00:20:06.430 --> 00:20:08.290
at your fingertips.

00:20:08.290 --> 00:20:11.090
Our quick navigation
tools in Presenter view

00:20:11.090 --> 00:20:14.320
allow you to quickly navigate
to any slide in your deck

00:20:14.320 --> 00:20:18.580
if you need to revisit a
specific point or visual.

00:20:18.580 --> 00:20:24.610
And at any time, you can
turn on a laser pointer

00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:27.660
to direct the attention
of your audience

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:30.070
to a certain part
of the presentation.

00:20:39.710 --> 00:20:42.750
In Presenter view,
you also have access

00:20:42.750 --> 00:20:45.540
to a feature unique
to Google Slides--

00:20:45.540 --> 00:20:49.830
Q&amp;A. With Q&amp;A, you can
better engage your audience

00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:52.830
by allowing them to
submit questions and vote

00:20:52.830 --> 00:20:57.130
on them during Google
Slides presentations.

00:20:57.130 --> 00:21:02.242
Once you start a Q&amp;A session,
Slides displays a unique URL

00:21:02.242 --> 00:21:06.100
that audience members can
go to and submit questions.

00:21:06.100 --> 00:21:08.770
You can decide when to
answer the questions

00:21:08.770 --> 00:21:12.810
and display them right on
the big screen, one by one.

00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:15.750
The audience members can
also vote on the questions

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:17.795
other people submit,
so you know where

00:21:17.795 --> 00:21:19.680
to focus your time
if you only have

00:21:19.680 --> 00:21:21.665
a few minutes for questions.

00:21:25.545 --> 00:21:29.080
This concludes the journey
of a typical presentation.

00:21:29.080 --> 00:21:32.170
I hope you learned about
some Slides features

00:21:32.170 --> 00:21:34.370
you may not have been aware of.

00:21:34.370 --> 00:21:36.340
And as a quick
recap, Slides helps

00:21:36.340 --> 00:21:40.500
you get started with tools
like templates and APIs.

00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:43.188
It facilitates
realtime collaboration

00:21:43.188 --> 00:21:46.640
with comments and action items.

00:21:46.640 --> 00:21:49.430
You can let Slides be your
personal designer with Slides

00:21:49.430 --> 00:21:51.070
Explore.

00:21:51.070 --> 00:21:55.838
And finally, you can have
confidence with Slides

00:21:55.838 --> 00:21:59.654
that help give you the power
to give a great presentation,

00:21:59.654 --> 00:22:02.970
and host a live Q&amp;A
with an audience.

00:22:02.970 --> 00:22:05.580
If you want to learn
more about Google Slides,

00:22:05.580 --> 00:22:10.040
you can visit the G
Suite Learning Center.

00:22:10.040 --> 00:22:11.410
That's a wrap for today.

00:22:11.410 --> 00:22:13.830
Please stay tuned
for a live Q&amp;A. We'll

00:22:13.830 --> 00:22:15.574
be back in less than a minute.

00:23:39.523 --> 00:23:40.064
Welcome back.

00:23:40.064 --> 00:23:42.022
We have a couple of
questions from the audience

00:23:42.022 --> 00:23:43.740
that I'd like to answer.

00:23:43.740 --> 00:23:46.574
The first question is,
after final creation,

00:23:46.574 --> 00:23:49.570
can Google Slides
work in offline mode?

00:23:49.570 --> 00:23:50.900
That's a great question.

00:23:50.900 --> 00:23:51.955
The answer's yes.

00:23:51.955 --> 00:23:55.134
In Google Slides, you can
make all of the slides files

00:23:55.134 --> 00:23:57.710
that you want available
in offline mode.

00:23:57.710 --> 00:23:59.650
And when you make
changes offline,

00:23:59.650 --> 00:24:01.780
as soon as you go back
online, those changes

00:24:01.780 --> 00:24:04.720
will be synced to the
presentation with all

00:24:04.720 --> 00:24:07.490
of your other collaborators.

00:24:07.490 --> 00:24:10.850
The next question is, can
I share a presentation

00:24:10.850 --> 00:24:15.200
I make in Slides with someone
without a G Suite account?

00:24:15.200 --> 00:24:15.890
Yes.

00:24:15.890 --> 00:24:18.500
There are actually a couple
ways you can do this.

00:24:18.500 --> 00:24:24.560
In Slides, you can share the
Present view of the slide deck

00:24:24.560 --> 00:24:25.760
and make that public.

00:24:25.760 --> 00:24:29.120
And this allows you to share
the content of your presentation

00:24:29.120 --> 00:24:31.620
with whoever you want.

00:24:31.620 --> 00:24:34.110
There's also ways to download
the content from Slides

00:24:34.110 --> 00:24:40.330
into multiple file types,
like PDF or PowerPoint.

00:24:40.330 --> 00:24:43.030
The next question is,
how can I prevent someone

00:24:43.030 --> 00:24:46.510
from making changes to a
presentation I sent to them?

00:24:46.510 --> 00:24:48.694
And how do I limit
access to a presentation

00:24:48.694 --> 00:24:51.466
so only people in my
company can see it?

00:24:51.466 --> 00:24:55.530
These are also great
questions, and important ones.

00:24:55.530 --> 00:24:58.310
So when you share
presentation in Google Slides,

00:24:58.310 --> 00:25:02.630
you have the option to provide
different levels of access.

00:25:02.630 --> 00:25:05.660
You can provide access to
edit, access to comment,

00:25:05.660 --> 00:25:07.580
and access to view.

00:25:07.580 --> 00:25:10.070
If you provide access to
edit, the collaborator

00:25:10.070 --> 00:25:12.742
can change whatever they
want in and decide with you.

00:25:12.742 --> 00:25:14.920
If you provide
access to comment,

00:25:14.920 --> 00:25:16.420
they can make
comments on the slide,

00:25:16.420 --> 00:25:18.760
but they can't make any changes.

00:25:18.760 --> 00:25:21.670
And if you provide
access to view,

00:25:21.670 --> 00:25:25.429
the recipient can only view
the contents of the deck.

00:25:25.429 --> 00:25:27.720
There is additional advanced
settings in the share menu

00:25:27.720 --> 00:25:31.410
that can even prevent you from
letting people copy contents

00:25:31.410 --> 00:25:33.890
from the slides to other decks.

00:25:33.890 --> 00:25:37.380
In terms of a limit of
access to presentations,

00:25:37.380 --> 00:25:39.875
so only people at your
company can see it,

00:25:39.875 --> 00:25:42.897
there are the main level
controls at the admin level

00:25:42.897 --> 00:25:45.149
that can be set, so
presentations can only

00:25:45.149 --> 00:25:49.280
be available within your domain.

00:25:49.280 --> 00:25:53.019
Can I add videos to my
slides is the next question.

00:25:53.019 --> 00:25:54.560
This is also a great
question, and we

00:25:54.560 --> 00:25:56.370
have two ways to do this.

00:25:56.370 --> 00:26:00.620
You can embed videos directly
from YouTube into your deck.

00:26:00.620 --> 00:26:03.640
And you can also upload
videos from Drive,

00:26:03.640 --> 00:26:06.010
that you may have saved
from a variety of sources,

00:26:06.010 --> 00:26:08.235
into your deck.

00:26:08.235 --> 00:26:11.350
And the last question
is, can I hide some

00:26:11.350 --> 00:26:13.510
slides when I'm presenting?

00:26:13.510 --> 00:26:16.210
This is actually a feature
we've just recently built,

00:26:16.210 --> 00:26:18.580
and it's called skip slides.

00:26:18.580 --> 00:26:23.100
When you're in the edit view of
Slides, on the left-hand side,

00:26:23.100 --> 00:26:24.474
there's a film strip.

00:26:24.474 --> 00:26:27.270
And if you right-click on
a slide in the film strip,

00:26:27.270 --> 00:26:29.940
you'll have the
option to skip slides.

00:26:29.940 --> 00:26:33.258
If you highlight a slide
and select skip slides,

00:26:33.258 --> 00:26:34.216
you'll see an eye icon.

00:26:34.216 --> 00:26:39.710
And that means when you present,
that slide will be skipped.

00:26:39.710 --> 00:26:42.060
It looks like that's
it for the questions.

00:26:42.060 --> 00:26:46.730
So in closing, you can stay
tuned for the next session, how

00:26:46.730 --> 00:26:50.720
Nest uses Google Cloud and
Tableau to drive its business.

00:26:50.720 --> 00:26:53.720
Thank you very
much for your time.

00:26:53.720 --> 00:26:57.070
[MUSIC PLAYING]

